Z||000004||GT Bastard||12-22-2000||08:20 AM||||I'm using a Kush-Lok solid disc(organic pad) from ACT.  According to 1FST2M6, the pad is more porous(disapates heat better) and it's mounted on a marcel plate that is supposed to flex and act as a spring(since it has no springs.) I wanted something more aggressive than kevlar. check them out at <A HREF="http://www.clutchnet.com" TARGET=_blank>www.clutchnet.com</A> <P>I've got the 4-puck unsprung disc right now(metal pads) and it's aggressive as hell! I can chirp the tires into 3rd with it pretty well.  I'm a little concerned for the flywheel and other parts of the drivetrain that are stressed by it. It also SUCKS in traffic.<P>ps-you can use stock pressure plates with ACT clutches.<p>[This message has been edited by GT Bastard (edited 12-22-2000).]||||reg||1
